      "problem": "Which of the graphs below represent proportional relationships?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14184158/assets/4cc220afc9f6b1f8752076d0b8d8233caec22e937c0579926439b39472be8c80.png)",
      "worked_solution": "Remember that the graph of a proportional relationship is always a straight line that passes through the origin $(0,0).$\n\nOf the given graphs, only graph II fits this description.\n\n- Graphs I and IV are not straight lines.\n\n- Graph III does not pass through the origin $(0,0).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\".",
